 function referencePage(){return `<p class="eyebrow">DESIGN NOTEBOOK / SOURCES</p><h1>What we’re learning from.</h1><p class="lead">A visible record of the references, useful patterns, and limits behind this showcase. Inspiration is not a claim of feature parity.</p><p class="micro">Research date: September 18, 2026. Earlier landscape entries retain their September 8 date.</p><div class="reference-grid">${designReferences.map(r=>`<article class="card"><div class="row"><h2><a href="${r.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${r.name} ↗</a></h2><span class="pill">${r.tag}</span></div><p><strong>Useful pattern:</strong> ${r.use}</p><p><strong>Here:</strong> ${r.here}</p><p class="micro"><strong>Evidence:</strong> ${r.evidence}</p></article>`).join('')}</div><section class="card" style="margin-top:24px"><h2>The wider landscape</h2><p>Earlier research also covered source tools, authoring, offline distribution, and review. These are historical research leads, not newly verified integrations.</p><details><summary>Show the earlier project directory</summary><ul class="reference-directory">${earlierReferences.map(r=>`<li><a href="${r.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${r.name} ↗</a></li>`).join('')}</ul></details><div class="action-row"><a class="text-link" href="REFERENCES.md">Readable reference index</a><a class="text-link" href="research/references.md">Full evidence and adoption notes</a></div></section>`;}
